					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														First off (Quiarrah pulls out a scroll and unrolls it, and it keeps going and going and going. . . )I would like to thank one person who is not with us anymore (a moment of silence) Richmond Ironblood for inviting me into this guild when I was a lowly 4th lvl character. I wanted to be in this guild when Sis Ti joined! They say you can't choose your family. . . well, I think I have choosen the best family I could. Thank you Uncle Rich, where ever you are.<br />
I would also like to thank Sozei for giving me the the Crystal covered Shroud when I was only like 8th lvl. Thank you hon, it's my favorite! I had a robe of the oracle, but that thing was pretty gaudy with the gold buttons on the bust!<br />
Sanadeb, my most favorite of Big Brothers in the guild has actually laid his life down for me at Unrest. You died right next to me, so close in fact that you weapon was &quot;piercing&quot; my heart! (hmmm,. . . ) Now that's love! Thanks San for fighting and dieing at my side. <br />
SB for the times that you raised me. . thank you.<br />
Ukari for making me an officer. . . he saw something, although I'm not quite sure what! <br />
If I'm forgetting anyone, please forgive me. . . I thank you all for the help that has been given. <br />
Whitespark, for  helping me achieve the big double 2! Thank you hon! So much, I could not have done it without you. <br />
(Hmmm, reads scroll.. .da,da,dada,da. . . )<br />
Oh and of course sister Ti for if not for her I wouldn't be here anyway!<br />
Thank you to those who have just been there  too. . .you know who you are. . . and of course a cute little woodelf who took good care of me. Please come back. <br />
Thank you everyone for a job well done. . . <br />
I believe I mentioned this once before but I will again before I go. . . with all the bickering we have had lately I think people need to be reminded. So before I go.. . . in the words of a famous scholar...(slight rewrite on my behalf) &quot;ask not what your guild can do for you, but what you can do for your guild&quot;. It appears that people come into guilds expecting to get things handed to them on a silver platter. . . and then they leave! I think perhaps we should change our way of thinking. . . and ask the question, &quot;What can I do for my guild and my fellow guildmates?&quot; As an officer I have not given of many &quot;things&quot;. . . but I have given of my time and have been there for people when they wanted or neede to talk. Remember, Counsolor Q's office is always open! Thank you. . . (bows, rolls up scroll and walks away with tears).<br />
(geez, I sound like I won an Oscar. . . )<br />
Love ya, see ya in the game!<br />
Q						</td>
